  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 120 PM CDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nThe upper shortwave trough will continue to interact with the\nmoist airmass making showers and thunderstorms likely Thursday\ninto early Friday. Models show PW 1.75-2.00 inches over the\nwestern half of our CWA which could lead to locally heavy rain.\nWPC has this area in the slight (Level 2 of 4) risk for rainfall\nto exceed flash flood guidance Thursday. The NBM is showing\nrainfall totals of 1-2 inches with isolated amounts up to 4\ninches. The highest totals will be over Val Verde County with a\nsharp drop off starting around Uvalde. Most of the CWA is below\n0.5 inch. Friday evening the upper shortwave will move away to the\nnortheast, there still may be enough lift for isolated showers\nFriday night and Saturday. Dry weather will return for Saturday\nnight and Sunday. Monday night and Tuesday a cold front will move\nthrough the region bringing another chance for rain. At this time,\nmodels are moving this boundary quickly with only moderate amounts\nof rain, but PW values are high enough that there could be some\nlocally heavy rain.\n\nWith cloudy skies and rain, temperatures will be cooler Thursday\nand Friday with highs mostly in the 70s. The weekend should be\nwarmer with less cloudiness and mainly dry weather. The cold front\nTuesday will bring a cooler airmass for the end of this period.",
